  <content>
    <section class="practice" id="sect-00001"><title>Warm Up Activity</title>
      <exercise id="exer-00001">
        <problem id="prob-00001">
        <para id="para-00001"><link class="os-embed" url="#exercise/Alg1_4_13_1_WU_80"/></para>
        </problem>
        </exercise>
       
       
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <note id="note-00001">
        <para id="para-00028">Building Character: Creativity</para>
          
            <media alt="Insert Alt Text">
              <image mime-type="image/png" src="../../media/Algebra-1_04_15_02_01.png" width="200"/>
            </media>
          
          
            <para id="para-00029">Despite the stereotype of the mad genius, everyday creativity is just as important. You can use it to help you improve your mood and cope with stress, feel more connected with other people and the world—and even help you find meaning and purpose in life.</para>
            <para id="para-00030">Think about your current sense of creativity. Are the following statements true for you??</para>
            <list id="list-00001">
              <item>
          I often make decisions that take me outside my comfort zone.
       </item>
              <item>
          I have a playful attitude toward learning something new.
       </item>
            </list>
            <para id="para-00031">Don’t worry if none of these statements are true for you. Developing this trait takes time. Your first step starts today!</para>
          
        
      </note>
    </section>
  </content>
